ays so difficult?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "As I told you, he's stubborn and blatantly unyielding."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I know that he went from a child to a teenager in a blink of an eye."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Stressing new Information"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Sentence stress gives English its <span class=\"strong\">rhythm</span> or \"beat\". "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Word stress is emphasis on <span class=\"strong\">one syllable</span> within a <span class=\"strong\">word</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Sentence stress is emphasis on <span class=\"strong\">certain words</span> within a <span class=\"strong\">sentence</span>."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Most sentences have two basic types of words:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">content words</span>  <li>Content words are the important or key words in a sentence. They provide the meaning of the sentence.</li>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">structure words </span>  <li>Structure words are not important words. They are small words that you use to make the sentence correct. </li>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Stressing New Information <br><br>You pronounce new information with more breath force, since it is more prominent. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Jim</span>: <span class=\"strong\">Where</span> are you <span class=\"strong\">going</span>?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Lucy</span>: I'm going to <span class=\"strong\">Boston</span>."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "kicked out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "asked to leave"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Uncle Edward kicked my cousin Nick out."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le01ob04aud01"}]}, {"type": "ta